{"title":"1976 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems from the <b>1976 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=United_States_of_America_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"United States of America Mathematical Olympiad\"> USAMO</a></b>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/0/bb023b115e30010d4f1daa300d792b67658733a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] void fillsq(int x, int y){    fill((x,y)--(x+1,y)--(x+1,y+1)--(x,y+1)--cycle, mediumgray); } int i; fillsq(1,0);fillsq(4,0);fillsq(6,0); fillsq(0,1);fillsq(1,1);fillsq(2,1);fillsq(4,1);fillsq(5,1); fillsq(0,2);fillsq(2,2);fillsq(4,2); fillsq(0,3);fillsq(1,3);fillsq(4,3);fillsq(5,3); for(i=0; i&lt;=7; ++i){draw((i,0)--(i,4),black+0.5);} for(i=0; i&lt;=4; ++i){draw((0,i)--(7,i),black+0.5);} draw((3,1)--(3,3)--(7,3)--(7,1)--cycle,black+1); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"145\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>(a) Suppose that each square of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a95909131c9ac3b6732a9378f813302632e63e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> chessboard, as shown above, is colored either black or white. Prove that with <i>any</i> such coloring, the board must contain a rectangle (formed by the horizontal and vertical lines of the board such as the one outlined in the figure) whose four distinct unit corner squares are all of the same color.</li>\n<li>(b) Exhibit a black-white coloring of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb7c3757856afc9cb53f1b2ca262a05aaeb96322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\times 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> board in which the four corner squares of every rectangle, as described above, are not all of the same color.</li></ul>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are fixed points on a given circle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7774174993ffa29a38cf577ae34d8e0a3a63cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is a variable diameter of the same circle, determine the locus of the point of intersection of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d857b2c804701b561a5c8c90c400f360d27232c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/2/ed2a785c017799008f04738684e86dba12bfbb28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BY$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />. You may assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is not a diameter.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2ee0dc899d7824f7648504e2e34196cd679264.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300); defaultpen(fontsize(8)); real r=10; picture pica, picb; pair A=r*expi(5*pi/6), B=r*expi(pi/6), X=r*expi(pi/3), X1=r*expi(-pi/12), Y=r*expi(4*pi/3), Y1=r*expi(11*pi/12), O=(0,0), P, P1; P = extension(A,X,B,Y);P1 = extension(A,X1,B,Y1); path circ1 = Circle((0,0),r);  draw(pica, circ1);draw(pica, B--A--P--Y--X);dot(pica,P^^O); label(pica,&quot;$A$&quot;,A,(-1,1));label(pica,&quot;$B$&quot;,B,(1,0));label(pica,&quot;$X$&quot;,X,(0,1));label(pica,&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,(0,-1));label(pica,&quot;$P$&quot;,P,(1,1));label(pica,&quot;$O$&quot;,O,(-1,1));label(pica,&quot;(a)&quot;,O+(0,-13),(0,0));  draw(picb, circ1);draw(picb, B--A--X1--Y1--B);dot(picb,P1^^O); label(picb,&quot;$A$&quot;,A,(-1,1));label(picb,&quot;$B$&quot;,B,(1,1));label(picb,&quot;$X$&quot;,X1,(1,-1));label(picb,&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y1,(-1,0));label(picb,&quot;$P&#39;$&quot;,P1,(-1,-1));label(picb,&quot;$O$&quot;,O,(-1,-1)); label(picb,&quot;(b)&quot;,O+(0,-13),(0,0));  add(pica); add(shift(30*right)*picb); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"258\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all integral solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6bba557f91086cf968e4f3232e1847764fb689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2=a^2b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the sum of the lengths of the six edges of a trirectangular tetrahedron <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f7171346ba14a05722c3b2a0954f59407eec9ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PABC$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> (i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4bd3fcb139562b5962f60f453c580bef7e0fc52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APB=\\angle BPC=\\angle CPA=90^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"266\" height=\"14\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, determine its maximum volume.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eeefa367883375994fd2e1f575d088bce9d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca59e861f7103ff5a48adc6c4521ad936504c772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> are all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomials</a> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7cd8a121a26324cfb87e8329bbd724c7792dcb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x^5) + xQ(x^5) + x^2 R(x^5) = (x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x +1) S(x),\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"20\" />\nprove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO\" title=\"1976 USAMO\">1976 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1976\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO\" title=\"1975 USAMO\">1975 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO\" title=\"1977 USAMO\">1977 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 158/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5043/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.686      1 -total\n 51.29%    6.507      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 47.01%    5.964      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7568:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024417 and revision id 53434. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}